  "goodToKnow": "Die Schmach is disgrace or humiliation, a literary and emotional word: eine Schmach erleiden, Schmach und Schande. In the Weimar Republic, nationalists called the 1919 Treaty of Versailles die Schmach von Versailles, a slogan exploited by the Nazis. Sports reports use it for crushing defeats. Schmählich means shameful, and schmähen to revile. It has no plural."
